From 6d835a8d4820465119807471d293a6335c91915c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cory Forsythe <cory@coryforsythe.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 09:34:44 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 13/24] fix(hermes-vps): bridge-mediated status/report/steering
 protocol

The remote VPS agent has no path back to this Mac's filesystem at all, so it
could not append its own status, write its report, read steering messages, or
even report that it was blocked - a broken dispatch produced no signal in
Firstmate at all. The local bridge now owns status (FIRSTMATE-STATUS sentinel
lines, validated against the fixed state vocabulary), report
(FIRSTMATE-REPORT-BEGIN/END blocks), and steering (polls and delivers the
inbox itself, swallowing the unreachable doorbell line) as a transport
concern instead of a filesystem one, with every protocol failure surfacing as
a bridge-authored status diagnostic rather than silence.

Live verification against the real VPS surfaced and fixed two additional
bugs: a select()/buffered-readline() mismatch that could strand an
already-buffered second stdin line for up to 30s, and message.complete's own
"text" field silently dropping an earlier text segment whenever a turn
interleaves text with a tool call (fixed by accumulating message.delta chunks
per turn instead).

bin/fm-brief.sh --harness hermes-vps scaffolds the worker-side protocol
instead of literal local shell commands, and routes the scout completion gate
to firstmate since the worker cannot read captain-hold-lifecycle or run
bin/fm-captain-hold.sh either.
